{% tool-context
   title="System Design Calculator"
   question="What is system sizing?"
   definition="System sizing turns product behavior into a capacity envelope: the traffic each tier must serve, the reserve it keeps, the data it stores, and the failures it can absorb."
   inputs="Model user demand and cache behavior, then provision benchmarked application and database capacity, headroom, failure domains, and storage replication."
   outcome="Trace requests from users to the data tier, compare demand with safe capacity, and identify the first bottleneck instead of relying on one headline server count."
   experiment="Create a healthy baseline, then inject a launch surge, cache outage, zone loss, slow data tier, or retry storm and recover the design by changing the relevant assumption." /%}

